because of event-time ordering, the timer in CoProcess might fire before all session windows for a job have emitted\n\nThe cleanest fix: Since the CoProcess receives session window outputs which have timestamps at the window end, and the job finish events also have timestamps, the timer at `timestamp + 1` will only fire when the watermark advances past that point. But multiple session windows for the same job can arrive at different event times, and the emitted flag would prevent later updates.\n\nLet me use a completely different, simpler approach: **batch-style processing**. Use Flink's DataSet API-like approach or simply accumulate everything in a ProcessFunction."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5154,"cache_read_input_tokens":59475,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5154,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtEmL7VRwzTVNTA7s7HY","type":"assistant","uuid":"c807764b-74b0-49df-b4e6-534506d17244","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:30:47.606Z"}
